# Keep end-user docs in sync with the UI

When you change anything that's **visible to end users** in `index.html`, `styles.css`, or `app.js`, you must also update the end-user documentation:

- `docs/what-feedmeter-does.md` — the doc that describes what users see and how to use the app.
- `docs/screenshots/` — the matching screenshot file(s). See `docs/screenshots/README.md` for the canonical filenames.

## What counts as a UI-visible change

**Triggers an update:**

- New, renamed, removed, or reordered buttons / tiles / tabs / modals.
- New settings, status fields, or stats on screen.
- Changed user-facing labels, placeholder text, or modal titles.
- New or changed user flows (e.g. a new prompt after an action).
- Layout restructures.

**Does not trigger an update:**

- Pure refactors that don't change anything visible.
- Sync, network, caching, offline-queue, or storage logic.
- Bug fixes that don't change wording or structure.
- CSS tweaks that don't change layout meaningfully (color polish, spacing).

## Workflow when you make a UI-visible change

1. **Edit `docs/what-feedmeter-does.md`** so the affected section still describes reality. Keep the tone friendly and concise — this doc is for non-technical family members.
2. **List the stale screenshots** in your reply to the user. Reference filenames from `docs/screenshots/README.md` (e.g. *"`bottle-save.png` and `home.png` need to be re-captured"*).
3. If the change introduces a **new screen, modal, or flow** that isn't covered yet:
   - Add a new row to the screenshot list in `docs/screenshots/README.md`.
   - Add a corresponding subsection to `docs/what-feedmeter-does.md`.
4. You **cannot retake screenshots yourself** — that's a manual step the user does. Just clearly call out which ones go stale so they can refresh them in the same change.

## Example callout

> Heads up: this change renames "Bottle" to "Feed" on the third tile and adds a new **Diaper** tile. I've updated `docs/what-feedmeter-does.md` accordingly. The following screenshots are now stale and need to be re-captured (see `docs/screenshots/README.md`):
>
> - `home.png` — shows the four tiles, layout changed.
> - `bottle-save.png` — modal title changed.
